<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ruleset name="hermiq"
    xmlns="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0 http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset_xml_schema.xsd">
    <description>hermiq — Conduction PHPMD ruleset (single source: conduction/hydra-gates).</description>

    <rule ref="vendor/conduction/hydra-gates/quality-config/phpmd.xml">
        <exclude name="StaticAccess"/>
        <exclude name="ShortVariable"/>
    </rule>

    <!-- StaticAccess: one exception, and only one.

         `\OCA\Hermiq\Support\FleetAppId` is a pure resolver over two constant
         maps: given a canonical app name it returns whichever id or namespace
         the instance actually has. It holds no state and no collaborators — it
         takes the only things it needs as arguments — so there is nothing here
         that could be injected. Making it a service would add DI wiring around
         a lookup table, and would have to reach the two call sites that need it
         before their own constructors run.

         It also exists to be DELETED. It bridges the window in which the fleet
         answers to both its old and its new app ids and namespaces; once those
         agree, every call site becomes a plain string again and the class goes.

         This uses the rule's OWN `exceptions` property — its designed
         configuration surface — rather than an @SuppressWarnings annotation or
         a baseline entry. The rule stays fully active for every other class,
         and the exception is one named class, visible in config, with the
         reason attached. Same shape as pipelinq's.

         SECOND EXCEPTION, added 2026-09-19:
         `\OCA\OpenRegister\Service\Capability\ToolGrantResolver`.
         `isWriteOrDestructive()` is declared `public static` by OpenRegister,
         its owner. hermiq cannot inject what another app declared static, and
         wrapping it would add an indirection whose only purpose is to satisfy
         a linter. Two call sites, both asking the same pure classification
         question of a tool id: IntakeToolGrant::createsOnly() and
         OutsideToolSurface::writes(). If OpenRegister ever makes it an
         instance method, delete this half of the exception and inject it. -->
    <!-- ShortVariable: the shared allowlist, plus `at`.

         Thirteen of this repository's findings are one identifier. `$at` is a
         DateTimeImmutable meaning "the moment this happened", declared as a
         parameter and passed by NAME at every call site (`at: $at`), so it
         reads as prose where it is used. Renaming it to reach three characters
         would rename the named-argument label at every caller in lib/ and in
         the tests, and a missed call site under named arguments is a RUNTIME
         TypeError, not something the analysers catch.

         ⚠️ `minimum` and the rest of `exceptions` are COPIED from
         conduction/hydra-gates' quality-config/phpmd.xml, because re-declaring
         a rule REPLACES its properties rather than merging them. Declaring
         only `exceptions="at"` reset `minimum` to the rule's own default and
         took this repository from 23 findings to 156. If the shared list
         changes, this copy has to change with it — which is the argument for
         adding `at` there instead, and deleting this block.
      -->
    <rule ref="rulesets/naming.xml/ShortVariable">
        <properties>
            <property name="minimum" value="3" />
            <property name="exceptions" value="id,db,qb,op,ui,io,gc,tz,pk,fk,to,ch,a,b,l,v,c,t,r,f,n,k,e,at" />
        </properties>
    </rule>

    <rule ref="rulesets/cleancode.xml/StaticAccess">
        <properties>
            <property name="exceptions" value="\OCA\Hermiq\Support\FleetAppId,\OCA\OpenRegister\Service\Capability\ToolGrantResolver"/>
        </properties>
    </rule>
</ruleset>
